Design Patterns are the well proved solution of commonly occuring problems in software Design

Singleton design Pattern - is used when we want to create only one object of a class during the entire programme like in 
 db connection and logger etc we need only one instance of a class

 In singleton 
 The constructor is private so no one can create the object directly.
 A static method is used to give the object.
 The object is created only once and then reused.

 example - suppose u are the CEO in a company, everyone talks to the same ceo, and we do not create new ceo each time
